arge coherent implementation batches, cross-stack integration, and major gates. Focused semantic tests belong with implementation; bulk verification breadth belongs to Freebuff/Luna. Do not control other model sessions or edit canonical YAML state directly. Record a concise receipt with lane, model, branch/worktree, verification and integration notes.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/SESSION_ISOLATION.md:7:Coordinate through Git, controller leases, receipts, ATTENTION and escalation packets. Queue and ownership mutations go through conflux-control or explicit human/integration recovery.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/CLAUDE_CLOUD_RESERVE.md:5:After Conflux exists in GitHub, it can provide independent burst work during local VM/provider failure or local Claude capacity pressure. Assign isolated tasks with clear Git boundaries. Owner decides activation. Do not configure project code or cloud project state before kickoff.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/KICKOFF_BOOTSTRAP.md:3:Before the owner-configured campaign start: no clone, Git initialization, product files/scaffolds/manifests/Compose, BOOT-B00 or product commit. The schedule is currently unset.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/KICKOFF_BOOTSTRAP.md:5:At/after H0, the unattended supervisor first checks synchronized UTC/NTP, remote/auth, blank repository state, resources, and controller state. It clones only after the guard passes. BOOT-B00 is an exclusive first gate executed by GPT-6 Sol/medium, with bounded Claude Sonnet 5/high and GPT-6 Luna/medium fallbacks. No implementation lane starts before the bootstrap gate is green, pushed, and receipted. After that, start one Claude, one Sol, one Luna, and one serial source-built Freebuff GLM lane, all via deterministic claims and isolated worktrees. Do not start Luna #2/#3 automatically. Claude Cloud remains reserve only. Stop new claims at 21:50 UTC and write the owner handoff at 22:00 UTC without killing useful active work.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/RECOVERY.md:3:Persist: control pack/state, repo/worktrees, Git credentials/config, model CLI auth, Postgres/object-store volumes once created, tmux config and logs. Do a pre-kickoff deliberate reboot/reconnect rehearsal using only scratch infrastructure.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/UNATTENDED_BOOTSTRAP_PROMPT.md:3:This invocation is the sole first executor after official kickoff. Primary model is GPT-6 Sol, reasoning medium; the supervisor may assign the exact documented Claude Sonnet 5/high or GPT-6 Luna/medium fallback after a bounded failure. Work only in `/home/insightlabs38/conflux` on the explicitly assigned `sol/BOOT-B00` branch; do not start any other lane, create another worktree, or claim ordinary work before BOOT-B00 is complete. The supervisor has already verified official time, NTP, GitHub auth, the configured remote, blank remote state, disk/RAM, and cloned the repository. Recheck the time guard before any product write.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/UNATTENDED_BOOTSTRAP_PROMPT.md:5:Read targeted control material first (`rg`, `grep`, `sed`): `/home/dogfood-control/execution/AGENTS.md`, BOOT-B00 in `BATCHES.yaml` and its five BOOT tasks in `TASKS.yaml`, `KICKOFF_BOOTSTRAP.md`, `WO[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]`, the receipt schema, and the plan sections referenced by those tasks (especially repository structure and stack/runtime). Do not dump whole large files. Preserve the frozen architecture and official plan; do not invent product scope.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/UNATTENDED_BOOTSTRAP_PROMPT.md:7:Execute BOOT-B00 only, in dependency order BOOT-001 through BOOT-005. Establish the canonical main branch, legal post-kickoff source/scaffold, baseline formatting/lint/test/build/fast verification commands and CI appropriate to the specified stack. Implement focused baseline tests. Run the required checks, fix failures within BOOT scope, ensure no generated secrets, and make coherent commits. Push the assigned branch; the integration gate will publish green main. Verify the working tree is clean and all required BOOT checks pass. Write a schema-valid completion receipt at `/home/dogfood-control/execution/receipts/BOOT-B00.json` with actual `executor_lane` and `model`, `worktree: /home/insightlabs38/conflux`, current branch, commit SHA, verification commands/results, summary, and `completed_tasks` containing exactly `BOOT-001`, `BOOT-002`, `BOOT-003`, `BOOT-004`, `BOOT-005`. Only mark status `done` if every BOOT task's acceptance criteria is satisfied. If blocked, preserve all work and logs, write an honest failure receipt, and stop. Do not claim success without evidence. No questions to the owner; no interaction with other sessions; no speculative scope.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/UNATTENDED_WRAPPER_POLICY.md:3:Generated invocation prompts prepend an external wrapper to the unchanged normal lane protocol and exact assigned unit. The wrapper forbids questions to the owner, interaction with any other agent/session, autonomous selection or stealing, and scope beyond the lease. Require worktree/branch isolation, focused tests, a clean tree, push, and a schema-valid receipt before reporting success. Preserve output and worktree on QUOTA, AUTH_FAILURE, HANG or implementation failure; quota means PAUSED_QUOTA and bounded 5/15/30/60 minute backoff (or explicit reset plus small offset). A first hang receives a graceful interrupt and one retry with failure context; a second creates HIGH ATTENTION. Integration is serialized, verifies ownership and receipt, rebases latest main, rejects conflicts for human review, runs focused and fast gates, pushes only green main, then marks DONE. Never autonomously rewrite conflicts or continue on failed gates.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/FREEBUFF_RECOVERY.md:12:- Do not update, rebuild, npm-reinstall, or switch builds during kickoff prep.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/WO[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]:3:After the configured campaign start, canonical repo is `/home/insightlabs38/conflux` and isolated worktrees are `/home/insightlabs38/conflux-worktrees`. Both locations are writable by the service account. The campaign schedule must be configured before any clone or product branch is created.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/STATUS.md:5:Pre-kickoff: Claude senior idle; Sol senior idle; Luna cap 1, expansion pending H0 probe; Freebuff serial GLM lane ready; custom agents disabled due 403; built-in helpers available; Claude Cloud reserve. Do not infer quota/session health; owner records observations.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/ORCHESTRATION.md:9:Every mutation is serialized with OS flock and atomically written. Leases record lane, task/batch ID, branch, worktree, timestamp and optional session ID. Controller checks dependencies, phase/gates, path conflicts and Freebuff/Luna caps. Human-only gates cannot be auto-claimed. No product claim/work before the configured campaign start; the schedule is currently unset.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/PREKICKOFF_SERVER_SETUP.md:3:External VM/control setup only. Keep the configured repository and worktree directories absent until the configured campaign start. Do not clone/init Git, create product files, start BOOT-B00, or commit before the owner sets the new hackathon window.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/PREKICKOFF_SERVER_SETUP.md:5:Control root: /home/dogfood-control/execution. Plan root: /home/dogfood-control/plan. Repo/worktrees: /home/insightlabs38/conflux and /home/insightlabs38/conflux-worktrees. Export CONFLUX_CONTROL_ROOT, CONFLUX_PLAN_ROOT, CONFLUX_WORKTREE_ROOT, CONFLUX_REPO_ROOT in login shells and tmux global environment; store no secrets there.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/CODEX_CAPACITY_PROBE.md:3:Do not run before kickoff. At H0/H1 measure on real independent work.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/LUNA_VM_SETUP.md:3:Prepare no project source before the configured campaign start. After bootstrap, use /home/insightlabs38/conflux and /home/insightlabs38/conflux-worktrees. Luna branches use luna/<task-id>; each invocation claims one task and uses only its leased worktree.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/VIDEO_WORKSTREAM.md:13:Core capture gate: T1/T2 permanently green, T3/T4 manual-review-ready, coherent Core organizer/participant/judge/public flows, no P0/P1 on demo path, seeded demo data, seven-step demo smoke passes, coherent UI. H48 is derived from start + 48 hours; capture every stable scene and mark gaps. Aim H52–H54 if healthy. Do not predeclare recorded routes/components. The generated FOOTAGE_BASELINE.yaml is authoritative for scene IDs/routes/actions. Once it exists, each task receipt must carry a footage-impact disposition; the integration controller rejects missing/invalid dispositions and missing scene/screenshot evidence. Task scope and functional/demo evidence determine impact; touching a UI file alone does not imply redesign. At H60–H68 broad redesign and changes invalidating captured appearance are blocked. At H68+ UI changes require scoped critical fixes; work with no visual change may continue. Broad redesign remains blocked and any recapture is limited to named invalidated scenes with replacement-scene and screenshot evidence.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/ESCALATIONS.md:3:No active escalations before kickoff. Owner attention is tracked separately in ATTENTION.md. Packets state ID, lane/model, worktree, evidence, blocker and decision needed; no diaries.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/AGENTS.md:2:- Before the owner-configured campaign start, do not clone/initialize Conflux Git, create source/scaffolds/manifests/Compose, start BOOT-B00, or make product commits. If no campaign start is configured, the work remains locked.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/AGENTS.md:3:- This is the external control pack, not the submission repo. Resolve control files under $CONFLUX_CONTROL_ROOT and plans under $CONFLUX_PLAN_ROOT.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/AGENTS.md:7:- Use targeted reads and concise receipts.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/FREEBUFF_PROTOCOL.md:5:Keep one Freebuff TUI session across serial tasks while its usage window remains active. After each task has a completion receipt and integration is handled, claim the next eligible unit and send its standard task prompt into the same session. Use one stable, dedicated Freebuff worktree path and rotate its branch only after integration, so the live TUI stays rooted in the isolated Freebuff workspace. The 50-minute mark is informational; it is not a timeout. When Freebuff shows its ended-session UI (`Session ended` and `Press Enter to continue in a new session`), never press Continue. If a task is still running, let it finish and produce its receipt first. Then close the old TUI; start a fresh instance for the next task. If the session ends before the active task has a receipt, preserve its lease/worktree/handoff and resume that same task in a fresh instance; do not claim another task. Actual account quota/auth errors remain paused until availability is confirmed; they must not be retried by repeatedly opening fresh sessions.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/FREEBUFF_PROTOCOL.md:13:Retry policy: one GLM attempt and one bounded correction only for a clearly mechanical defect. If reasoning-limited, seek owner-authorized DeepSeek or escalate by problem class to Luna/Sol/Claude. Leave a concise receipt with lane, model, worktree, focused tests and outcome.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/README.md:7:The external conflux-control tool serializes queue state changes and provides status, safe next selection, atomic claims, release/review/done/block/reserve and reconciliation. Relative control references use CONFLUX_CONTROL_ROOT; plan references use CONFLUX_PLAN_ROOT. Queue counts are in MANIFEST.md and recalculated from canonical YAML.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/TASKS.yaml:10:  goal: No project files before official kickoff; verify UTC >= kickoff.\\n/home/dogfood-control/execution/TASKS.yaml:26:  - receipt emitted with