{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,150p' /home/dogfood-control/plan/03_ARCHITECTURE.md; sed -n '1,90p' /home/dogfood-control/plan/00_EXECUTIVE_FREEZE.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,150p' /home/dogfood-control/plan/03_ARCHITECTURE.md; sed -n '1,90p' /home/dogfood-control/plan/00_EXECUTIVE_FREEZE.md\"","aggregated_output":"# System Architecture\n\n## Style\n\nA modular monolith is the deployment and transaction boundary. Domain modules are separated by explicit services/contracts, not by network calls.\n\n## Request/mutation path\n\n`UI or external client → REST endpoint/application command → authentication/authorization → policy/gate evaluation → transaction → domain mutation + AuditEvent + DomainEvent(outbox) → commit → async side effects`.\n\nNo email, webhook call, Git provider request, remote validation or large object transfer may occur inside deadline-sensitive DB transactions.\n\n## Runtime topology\n\n`Caddy → Django/ASGI + built React assets`, with PostgreSQL, Valkey, Celery worker and RustFS as primary local S3-compatible storage in the offline Compose stack; SeaweedFS runs only in a compatibility-test profile.\n\n## Source of truth\n\n- PostgreSQL: all authoritative business state.\n- object store: artifact bytes referenced by authoritative DB metadata; RustFS is primary offline service, SeaweedFS is the compatibility-test profile.\n- Valkey: disposable cache/rate-limit/broker data only.\n- outbox: durable async intent until delivery.\n\n## Extensibility\n\nUse code-level strategy/registry interfaces rather than generic runtime plugins:\n- PolicyFactProvider / safe PolicyOperator\n- StageTemplate / AdvancementStrategy\n- FormFieldType\n- ArtifactType / ArtifactValidator\n- AssignmentStrategy / BallotStrategy / AggregationStrategy\n- AwardSelectionStrategy / PrizeComponentType\n- PageBlockType\n- NotificationChannel\n- Importer / Exporter\n- RecordSigner\n\nAdding Stretch should normally mean registering a new strategy/type/UI schema, not altering foundational tables.\n\n## Public rendering acceptance\n\nAt least the gallery first page is returned with fixture title text present in raw HTML so the stdlib checker can verify it without JavaScript. React may hydrate/enhance the page afterward.\n\n## No event sourcing\n\nAudit and outbox records are evidence/integration infrastructure, not the source of truth. Current relational state remains canonical.\n# Executive Freeze\n\n## Frozen product model\n\nAn event is a staged competition workflow. Participants move through a Stage DAG; executable Policies and Temporal Gates govern actions; versioned Forms and typed Artifacts collect evidence; durable Projects accumulate identity while stage-specific Submissions freeze evidence; EvaluationPlans assign and aggregate judging; Awards consume results; Presentation composes the public site; all mutations flow through one application/API boundary with audit/outbox evidence.\n\n## Frozen architecture\n\n- Django 5.2 LTS + DRF modular monolith.\n- PostgreSQL is authoritative state.\n- React + TypeScript + Vite frontend.\n- Valkey is disposable cache/broker state only.\n- Celery for asynchronous jobs.\n- Generic S3-compatible object-storage adapter; RustFS is the primary offline object store in Compose. SeaweedFS is the required compatibility target; ZeroS3 is optional and noncritical.\n- Caddy reverse proxy.\n- REST `/api/v1` application boundary; frontend uses the same domain/application path as external clients.\n- Transactional outbox + readable AuditEvent log.\n- Stable public IDs; normal relational DB keys remain internal.\n\n## Frozen domain boundaries\n\nKeep distinct:\n\n- Workspace / Event\n- identity / membership / role assignment\n- Stage / StageEntry\n- Project / Submission / SubmissionVersion\n- Policy / TemporalGate / ExceptionGrant\n- FormDefinition / immutable FormVersion / responses\n- Artifact / upload intent / validators\n- EvaluationPlan / assignment / ballot / aggregation\n- Award / PrizePackage / fulfillment\n- Theme / Page / PageBlock\n\n## Scope strategy\n\n1. T1–T4 are mandatory Core milestones.\n2. Core continues beyond T4 to include multi-stage workflow, policies, typed evidence, normalization-aware judging, event templates, preflight, operations, portability, launch checks, upgrade/backup discipline, and polished builders.\n3. Normalization Proof, API First, and Threat Model are natural Core outputs. Pairwise is Stretch #1 because bonuses are tie-breakers rather than score additions.\n4. Stretch can be promoted whenever Core gates are green and integration/review capacity is healthy.\n5. Very Stretch is intentionally large but contains only features with material organizer/participant/judge/adoption value.\n\n## Red lines\n\nDo not add generic BPM/workflow infrastructure, event sourcing, microservices/Kafka, arbitrary organizer code/JS/SQL, AI judging, blockchain/provenance theater, fake confidence scores, payment/KYC/tax, source-control hosting, or an Internet plugin marketplace.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
